# Copy to `.env` if you need to override anything. Vite only exposes
# variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser bundle.
#
# You normally do NOT need to set anything here.
#
# By default the app calls the relative path /api ("same origin as this
# page"), and that gets forwarded to the Flask backend by:
#   - Vite's dev-server proxy in development  (see vite.config.js)
#   - nginx or IIS in production              (see nginx.conf)
#
# Because of that, the backend's host and port are not baked into the
# bundle, and CORS is not involved at all. To point the dev proxy at a
# backend on a different port, set API_PROXY_TARGET when starting Vite
# (a plain shell variable, not a VITE_ one):
#
#   API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8010 npm run dev
#
# Set VITE_API_BASE_URL ONLY for a deployment where the API really does live
# on a different origin than the frontend -- and make sure the backend's
# CORS_ORIGINS allows this frontend's origin in that case.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://assets.example.com/api
